= Yi Jing — Hexagram Identifier =

A graphical **Tcl/Tk** tool for identifying I Ching hexagrams by toggling yin and yang lines.
Left-click any line to switch between solid (yang) and broken (yin).
Right-click a line to mark it as a **changing line** (mutation): ○ on yang, × on yin.
The hexagram number and its description update in real time.

== Quick start ==

{{{
wish hexagrams.tcl
}}}

Requires **Tcl/Tk 8.5+** ({{{sudo apt install tk}}} on Debian/Ubuntu).
For CJK characters in the trigram panel: {{{sudo apt install fonts-noto-cjk}}}.

== Features ==

* Six lines — **left-click** to toggle yang (solid) / yin (broken)
* **Right-click** to mark a changing line: ○ on yang (old yang), × on yin (old yin)
* Real-time hexagram identification (King Wen sequence, 1-64)
* Left panel with the hexagram's title, keywords and description
* Right trigram panel showing, for each of the two trigrams:
** Unicode trigram symbol (☰ … ☷)
** Chinese character (乾 坤 震 …)
** Pinyin name with tones (Qián, Kūn, Zhèn …)
** Translation in the active language
* **Three themes** — //light//, //dark//, //sepia// (default)
* **Three languages** — French, English and Chinese (简体中文)
* Hamburger menu ☰ (top right) — language, theme, reset
* Reset clears all mutations and returns to hexagram 1 (Qián)

== Files ==

{{{
hexagrams/
├── hexagrams.tcl          main application (single Tcl/Tk file)
├── hexagrams.fr.creole    hexagram descriptions in French
├── hexagrams.creole       hexagram descriptions in English
├── hexagrams.zh.creole    hexagram descriptions in Chinese (simplified)
├── README.creole          this file
├── CLAUDE.md              developer notes (architecture, theme keys)
└── .claude/skills/
    └── run-hexagrams.md   launch & verification checklist
}}}

== Configuration ==

Two variables at the top of {{{hexagrams.tcl}}} control the defaults:

{{{
set lang           "fr"    ;# "fr", "en" or "zh"
set ::current_theme "sepia" ;# "light", "dark" or "sepia"
}}}

== Data format (creole) ==

Hexagram descriptions follow a simple creole markup:

{{{
== 1. ䷀ ==

**Creativity, Heaven, Initiative**
//Creative force of heaven, absolute and active beginning.//
}}}

* {{{== N. … ==}}} — title (displayed at top of info panel, bold and coloured)
* {{{**…**}}} — bold keywords
* {{{//…//}}} — italic description

== Mutations ==

A **changing line** (爻变, yáo biàn) marks a line that transforms into its opposite,
producing a second (resulting) hexagram.

Right-click any line to toggle its mutation marker:

* **○** (old yang, 老阳) — solid line that will become yin
* **×** (old yin, 老阴) — broken line that will become yang

Mutation markers are independent of the line type and are cleared by Reset.

== Adding a theme ==

In {{{hexagrams.tcl}}}, add a new entry to {{{::themes}}} with all eleven colour keys,
then append the name to the theme submenu loop:

{{{
set ::themes(mytheme) {
    bg         #...   bg_left    #...   fg         #...
    fg2        #...   sep        #...   line       #...
    tri_bg     #...   tri_border #...   accent     #...
    btn_bg     #...   btn_fg     #...
}

foreach th {light dark sepia mytheme} { ... }
}}}

== Hexagram lookup ==

Each hexagram is identified by two trigrams (lower: lines 1-3, upper: lines 4-6).
The trigram value is computed as {{{l1 + l2×2 + l3×4}}} (yang = 1, bottom to top),
giving a number 0-7. The 64-entry lookup table is indexed by {{{upper×8 + lower}}}.

| Value | Trigram | Symbol | Pinyin |
| 0 | Kun  | ☷ | Kūn  |
| 1 | Zhen | ☳ | Zhèn |
| 2 | Kan  | ☵ | Kǎn  |
| 3 | Dui  | ☱ | Duì  |
| 4 | Gen  | ☶ | Gèn  |
| 5 | Li   | ☲ | Lí   |
| 6 | Xun  | ☴ | Xùn  |
| 7 | Qian | ☰ | Qián |

== Roadmap ==

=== HTML/JS version ===

A browser port is planned as a single self-contained {{{hexagrams.html}}} file
(no server, no build step, works offline).

The {{{.creole}}} data files and all hexagram logic port directly.
The main mapping is:

* Tcl canvas → HTML5 {{{<canvas>}}} + 2D context
* Theme system → CSS custom properties ({{{--accent}}}, {{{--bg}}}, …)
* Info panel → {{{<div>}}} with styled {{{<span>}}} elements
* Left-click / right-click → {{{click}}} / {{{contextmenu}}} events
* On mobile, right-click (mutations) would need a long-press fallback

Estimated scope: ~350 lines of vanilla HTML/CSS/JS.

